course: dictionary
lesson: 9925
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. You work out which meaning the writer wants by looking at the words around it. The word «tank» is a good example because it has several meanings.
explain: «A submarine fills its tanks with water to sink.» The clues are submarine and water, so a tank here is a big container that holds liquid. Ask yourself which meaning fits, then put your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: «Tank sniffs his hand, grumbles and lies down.» Tank has a capital letter and does things a dog does, so it is a name, not a container. Capital letters and the actions around a word are clues. The same spelling can mean something different.
fact: A tank is a big container that holds water, fuel, oil or gas.
fact: A fish tank is a glass box for fish.
fact: A tank can also be a big, heavy army vehicle with a gun that moves on metal tracks.
fact: A think tank is a group of people who think up ideas.
fact: In maths, the volume of a box-shaped tank is length × width × height.
exercise: «Watch a pet goldfish when you walk up to the tank: it swims to the front.» What is a tank here? | A group of people who think up ideas | *A glass box for fish | A shirt with no sleeves | A big army vehicle
exercise: «In 1970 an oxygen tank exploded on Apollo 13 on the way to the Moon.» What does tank mean? | A think tank of scientists | A fish tank in a classroom | A big army vehicle with a gun | *A container that holds gas
exercise: «Tank isn't wicked.» Why is Tank not a container here? | *Because it has a capital letter and is the name of a pet | Because containers are never wicked | Because a tank is always full | Because a tank only holds water
test: What is a think tank? | A shirt with no sleeves | A big heavy vehicle with a gun | *A group of people who think up ideas | A big container for petrol
test: A box-shaped tank is 2 metres long, 1 metre wide and 1 metre high. What is its volume? | 3 cubic metres | 4 cubic metres | *2 cubic metres | 1 cubic metre
exam: Which sentence uses tank as a container? | «Tank sniffs his hand, grumbles and lies down.» | «Tank isn't wicked.» | *«The petrol tank of the car is nearly empty.» | «Watch the goldfish swim to the front.»
